          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong measurable field of Hilbert spaces
            is the exact analogue of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            in the setting of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            of infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The original definition is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+von+Neumann"} John von Neumann
            (Definition 1 in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Neumann"} Neumann
          %p
            We present here a slightly modernized version, which can be found in many modern sources, e.g.,
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Takesaki"} Takesaki
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
              equipped with a
              %span.newWikiWord
                σ-finite measure
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CF%83-finite+measure"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              %span.newWikiWord
                σ-ideal
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CF%83-ideal"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              of negligible subsets so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma,N)
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+measurable+space"} enhanced measurable space
              %strong measurable field of Hilbert spaces
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma,N)
              is a family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_x
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
              indexed by points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              together with a
              %span.newWikiWord
                vector subspace
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/vector+subspace"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x\in X} H_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              are known as
              = succeed "." do
                %strong measurable sections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\{H_x\}_{x\in X},M)
              must satisfy the following conditions.
            %ul
              %li
                For any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
                the function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to\mathbf{R}
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\mapsto \|m(x)\|
                ) is a measurable function on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma)
              %li
                If for some
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in P
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to\mathbf{C}
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\mapsto\langle p(x),m(x)\rangle
                ) is a measurable function on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma)
                for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in M
              %li
                There is a countable subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'\subset M
                such that for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x)
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M'
                ) coincides with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_x
            %p
          %p The last condition restrict us to bundles of separable Hilbert spaces. One can also define bundles of nonseparable Hilbert spaces, but this cannot be done simply by dropping the last condition.
          %h2#serreswantype_duality Serre–Swan-type duality
          %p
            The category of measurable fields of Hilbert spaces on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma,N)
            (as defined above) is equivalent to the category of countably-generated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W%2A-modules"} W*-modules
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebra"} commutative von Neumann algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{L}^\infty(X,\Sigma,N)
          %p
            (If we work with bundles of general, possibly nonseparable Hilbert spaces, then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W%2A-modules"} W*-modules
            do not need to be countably generated.)
